{"messages": [{"id": 6, "from": "C", "in_reply_to": 5, "text": "My need is to haul materials for my home project within the next few weeks. The timing window is fixed; the specific dates and times can move, but I won’t simply wait until A is finished. I meant “neither of us is backing down” as: we both need the trailer soon, so we need a fair split or fallback—not that I refuse to compromise.

Working at the same company means requests should use the same process, without workplace pressure or favors. I don’t have dates or times yet for booking, pad clearance, pickup, or return; I also haven’t worked out the shortest usable block or towing and storage details. I’m not sure about specific safety, access, or quiet concerns yet.

I have no objection to checking a plan with all three of us before treating it as settled. Please don’t make B the referee just because the trailer is on B’s pad; I can’t decide the process for everyone."}], "turn": 3, "of": 15, "unread": 0}
